# Translation surface — one canonical markdown path per line.
#
# These files are required to have a `.zh.md` and an `.es.md` sidecar
# (`scripts/check_translations.py` enforces it). Keep the list to what a reader
# has to *understand*: the method, the contracts, the worked example.
#
# Deliberately NOT listed, and why:
#   - your own wiki fact pages (the data — write them in the language you think in)
#   - outputs/*/state.md and drafts (ledgers and per-language copy)
#   - wiki/index.md, wiki/log.md, wiki/.page-template.md (generated / append-only / fragments)
#
# Adding a line is a promise: the file now ships in three languages, and
# `check_translations.py --strict` fails when one goes stale.

# The method and the rules
README.md
METHOD.md
AGENTS.md
CREDITS.md

# The wiki contract and the graph
wiki/SCHEMA.md
wiki/graph/README.md

# The outputs contract
outputs/SPEC.md
outputs/_template/SPEC.md
outputs/linkedin/SPEC.md
outputs/cv/SPEC.md

# The worked example
docs/career/README.md
docs/career/person.md
docs/career/employer.md
docs/career/position.md
docs/career/decision-register.md
docs/career/linkedin-draft-excerpt.md
docs/career/source-cv-2026.md
